messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Narrow artificial general intelligence achieves human-level performance across most economic and cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "AI systems automate complex knowledge work, triggering rapid productivity growth alongside significant labor displacement and geopolitical competition over advanced compute."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Global carbon emissions peak and begin a sustained decline due to renewable energy scaling and carbon capture deployment.",
      "detail": "Solar and wind become the cheapest energy sources worldwide, while direct air capture facilities begin removing gigatons of CO2 from the atmosphere annually."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "First commercial fusion power plants begin delivering baseload electricity to national grids.",
      "detail": "Magnetic confinement fusion achieves reliable net energy gain at industrial scale, effectively ending the fossil fuel era for power generation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "First anti-aging therapies that meaningfully extend healthy human lifespan receive regulatory approval.",
      "detail": "Senolytics and partial cellular reprogramming extend healthspan by 5-10 years, accelerating demographic shifts toward longer-lived, aging populations."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "Autonomous AI and robotics manage the majority of global logistics, manufacturing, and agriculture.",
      "detail": "Human labor shifts predominantly to creative, care, and oversight roles, prompting widespread adoption of universal basic income and post-scarcity economic models."
    },
    {
      "year": 2062,
      "event": "Intensifying climate impacts cause mass migration and trillions in economic damage, but technological adaptation prevents civilizational collapse.",
      "detail": "Coastal flooding and agricultural disruption displace hundreds of millions, leading to massive sea walls and controlled-environment farming, while carbon removal stabilizes temperatures around +2°C."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "Planetary defense systems achieve reliable capability to deflect asteroids larger than one kilometer.",
      "detail": "Kinetic impactors and gravity tractors are deployed globally, effectively eliminating the existential threat of large asteroid impacts."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "First generation of humans born with germline genetic edits for disease resistance and cognitive enhancement reaches adulthood.",
      "detail": "Heritable genetic modification becomes available to wealthy populations, creating a genetic divide and sparking international treaties attempting to regulate human germline editing."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Brain-computer interfaces become ubiquitous, enabling direct neural access to digital networks and communication.",
      "detail": "Both invasive and non-invasive BCIs allow thought-based control and high-bandwidth mind-to-machine interaction, blurring the boundary between biological and digital cognition."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Global human population peaks at approximately 10 billion before beginning a gradual long-term decline.",
      "detail": "Fertility rates fall below replacement in most regions, creating aging societies that depend on automation, immigration, and extended lifespans to maintain economic output."
    },
    {
      "year": 2115,
      "event": "First self-sustaining orbital habitats house 100,000 people in Earth orbit.",
      "detail": "O'Neill cylinders and similar megastructures provide living space and zero-gravity manufacturing capacity, utilizing materials mined from near-Earth asteroids."
    },
    {
      "year": 2130,
      "event": "Artificial superintelligence is safely integrated into global infrastructure, science, and governance.",
      "detail": "ASI systems design new materials, medical treatments, and energy systems orders of magnitude faster than humans, while robust alignment protocols keep them within human-value constraints."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Mars population reaches one million with the beginning of atmospheric terraforming projects.",
      "detail": "Underground cities expand into surface domes, and genetically engineered organisms begin thickening the Martian atmosphere, though full terraforming remains centuries away."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "Asteroid mining makes platinum-group metals and rare earth elements abundant on Earth.",
      "detail": "Metal-rich asteroids are captured and processed in orbit, crashing global commodity prices and enabling new industrial and energy applications."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "First interstellar probe using laser-pushed light sails launches toward Proxima Centauri.",
      "detail": "A gram-scale probe accelerates to 0.2c, reaching the nearest star system in about 20 years while carrying human knowledge, genetic data, and uploaded consciousnesses."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Consciousness uploading becomes commercially available, allowing human minds to run on digital substrates.",
      "detail": "Whole brain emulation enables digital immortality and existence at variable speeds, though philosophical debates about personal identity and legal rights of uploads persist."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "The majority of human-descended minds exist as digital or hybrid entities in space habitats rather than on Earth.",
      "detail": "Biological humans become a minority, living in preserved nature reserves or as uploads, while civilization operates primarily in virtual environments and orbital megastructures."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Construction of a Dyson swarm begins around the Sun to capture a significant fraction of its energy.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating robots and disassembled asteroid material build solar collectors, marking the beginning of stellar-scale energy harvesting."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "First permanent extrasolar colony is established on a habitable planet orbiting Proxima Centauri or another nearby star.",
      "detail": "Human-descended intelligence becomes a multi-stellar species, with colonies established via generation ships, relativistic probes carrying uploads, or in-situ manufacturing from local materials."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization spans ten star systems with distinct local cultures and adaptations.",
      "detail": "Colonies around red dwarf stars utilize local resources and develop independently, beginning genetic and cultural divergence from Earth-origin populations."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Post-human speciation produces multiple distinct intelligent species that can no longer interbreed with baseline humans.",
      "detail": "Radical genetic engineering, cybernetic integration, and digital existence create branches of humanity with incompatible biologies and cognitive architectures."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Human-descended civilization controls one hundred star systems across the local stellar neighborhood.",
      "detail": "Expansion accelerates through self-replicating von Neumann probes that prepare systems for biological or digital settlement before colony ships arrive."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "A Kardashev Type II civilization is achieved, harnessing the total energy output of a star via a complete Dyson sphere.",
      "detail": "Stellar-scale engineering allows the civilization to manipulate its host star, providing virtually unlimited energy for computation and megastructure construction."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "One thousand star systems are inhabited by human-descended intelligences.",
      "detail": "The civilization has expanded throughout a significant portion of the Milky Way's habitable zone, with diverse societies adapted to different stellar and planetary environments."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "First definitive detection of an extraterrestrial technological civilization, confirming intelligent life is not unique.",
      "detail": "Dyson sphere infrared signatures or artificial radio signals are detected from another star system, triggering a galaxy-wide effort to establish communication and exchange knowledge."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Stellar engineering projects relocate solar systems to safer orbits or cluster them for resource efficiency.",
      "detail": "Shkadov thrusters or other megastructures move stars over millions of years, demonstrating control over stellar dynamics to avoid supernovae or optimize galactic real estate."
    },
    {
      "year": 7000,
      "event": "Matrioshka brains surround ten percent of stars in the local galactic neighborhood.",
      "detail": "Computational megastructures the size of solar systems convert stellar energy entirely into processing power, creating planet-sized thinking machines of immense capacity."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "A galaxy-wide communication network connects human-descended civilizations across the Milky Way.",
      "detail": "Laser relays and possibly quantum communication links transmit information across light-years, creating a shared galactic culture despite the impossibility of faster-than-light travel."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilizations control ten thousand star systems spanning the galactic disk.",
      "detail": "The expansion front reaches the outer rim of the galaxy, with civilizations adapting to the low-metallicity environments of the galactic halo."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Post-human civilization exists across fifty thousand star systems, while baseline biological Homo sapiens are extinct or preserved only in reserves.",
      "detail": "Humanity has fragmented into thousands of descendant species—digital, synthetic, and biologically modified—that consider themselves heirs to the original human project, though the original species no longer exists in the wild."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Over the next ten millennia, humanity likely survives the dangerous 21st and 22nd centuries—navigating climate change, AI alignment, and geopolitical conflict—to become a spacefaring, post-biological civilization spread across thousands of star systems. By 10000, baseline Homo sapiens will almost certainly be extinct or radically transformed into diverse descendant intelligences, making the question of whether 'humanity' still exists dependent on whether one defines it by species continuity or by civilizational lineage. If the species survives the next few centuries, it probably persists indefinitely in some form, but there remains a substantial risk of extinction before 2500 from existential threats."
}
